{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-12T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Just north of Moab, Utah, Arches National Park is home to more than 2,000 natural sandstone arches – the densest concentration of arches in the world. Today's image, North Window, is one of the best-known formations in the park's Windows Section, where towering fins, openings and sculpted sandstone create a landscape that looks almost architectural.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_EN-IN3919602543_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_EN-IN3919602543_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Architecture without an architect","Title":"North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/38.6857117,-109.5328291/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=38.6857117,-109.5328291;S9;North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Arches+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261111_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow"},"Ssd":"20261112","Name":"NorthWindow","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"3919602543","FullDateString":"12 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Atlantic Forest is one of the world's great biodiversity hotspots, stretching along much of Brazil's Atlantic coast and into Argentina and Paraguay. Its landscape includes tropical and subtropical forests, mangroves and coastal habitats, providing a home for around 20,000 plant species and an extraordinary variety of wildlife, including jaguars and golden lion tamarins. Much of the forest has disappeared over the centuries, but it continues to play an important role in storing carbon and providing fresh water for millions of people across the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_EN-IN3149189379_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_EN-IN3149189379_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A forest full of wonder","Title":"The Atlantic Forest, Brazil","Copyright":"© FG Trade/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Atlantic Forest is home to around 150 million people, which is roughly a third of South America's total population.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Atlantic+Forest+Brazil&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261110_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica"},"Ssd":"20261111","Name":"Atlantica","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"3149189379","FullDateString":"11 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Rose Island looks like a brushstroke of green surrounded by every shade of blue. Just five kilometres east of Paradise Island in The Bahamas, this slender cay trades busy roads and city blocks for sandy shores, shallow waters and an inland lagoon. Its peaceful appearance comes with a touch of movie drama. Rose Island was used as a filming location for the 1965 James Bond adventure 'Thunderball', including the explosive destruction of the Disco Volante.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_EN-IN1259562642_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_EN-IN1259562642_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Licensed to chill","Title":"Aerial view of Rose Island, The Bahamas","Copyright":"© Abstract Aerial Art/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/25.088243,-77.225304/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=25.088243,-77.225304;S9;Rose Island, The Bahamas&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rose+Island+Bahamas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261109_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland"},"Ssd":"20261110","Name":"RoseIsland","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"1259562642","FullDateString":"10 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Cross the Guadalquivir River in Seville, the capital of Spain's Andalusia region, and the city's rhythm seems to change. On the other side lies Triana, a colourful neighbourhood where ceramics, flamenco and local traditions are woven into everyday life. Since the 19th century, the Isabel II Bridge, also known as the Triana Bridge, has connected the neighbourhood to Seville's historic centre.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_EN-IN5231956941_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_EN-IN5231956941_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where art finds its rhythm","Title":"Historic district of Triana, Seville, Spain","Copyright":"© Andrzej Rostek/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.382904,-6.006341/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.382904,-6.006341;S9;Triana, Seville, Spain&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Seville+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261108_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain"},"Ssd":"20261109","Name":"TrianaSpain","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"5231956941","FullDateString":"9 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Across India, Diwali brings homes, streets and neighbourhoods to life with the warm glow of lanterns, diyas and colourful decorations. Known as the Festival of Lights, it celebrates themes of hope, new beginnings and the triumph of light over darkness. Traditions vary across the country, but for many families, the festivities include creating rangoli, performing Lakshmi Puja, exchanging sweets and gifts, and spending time with loved ones. Diwali is also associated with Lord Rama's return to Ayodhya after defeating Ravana. More than a festival, it's a time for togetherness, reflection and welcoming the year ahead with optimism.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DiwaliLamps_EN-IN0900276687_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DiwaliLamps_EN-IN0900276687_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Happy Diwali!","Title":"Lanterns for Diwali in Mumbai, Maharashtra","Copyright":"© Dinodia Photo/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/18.969048,72.821182/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=18.969048,72.821182;S9;Mumbai, Maharashtra&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261108_DiwaliLamps\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Diwali&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261107_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261108_DiwaliLamps"},"Ssd":"20261108","Name":"DiwaliLamps","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0900276687","FullDateString":"8 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bison are among the largest land mammals in the world, capable of weighing up to 900 kilograms and reaching speeds of 65 kilometres per hour despite their massive size. Despite often being called a buffalo, the American bison is not one of the true buffaloes, which are native to Africa and Asia. Its scientific name, Bison bison, leaves little room for confusion.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_EN-IN0635434875_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_EN-IN0635434875_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Roaming the grasslands","Title":"A bison in the grasslands of Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota, USA","Copyright":"© Tandem Stock/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/47.275714,-103.463282/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=47.275714,-103.463282;S9;Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=American+bison&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261106_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison"},"Ssd":"20261107","Name":"DakotaBison","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0635434875","FullDateString":"7 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A volcano, a rainforest and a bamboo grove? Haleakalā National Park on Maui has all three. Spanning Maui from its 3,055-metre summit to the coast, the park protects landscapes that change dramatically with elevation, rainfall and temperature. It was established in 1916 as part of Hawaii National Park and became its own national park in 1961. The name Haleakalā translates to 'House of the Sun', reflecting the Hawaiian mo'olelo of Māui capturing the Sun to lengthen the day.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-IN0566152296_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-IN0566152296_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A green tunnel through Maui","Title":"Bamboo forest, Pīpīwai Trail, Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© MNStudio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/20.760987,-156.155095/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=20.760987,-156.155095;S9;Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Haleakala+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261105_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail"},"Ssd":"20261106","Name":"PipiwaiTrail","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0566152296","FullDateString":"6 Nov, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"It's World Philosophy Day, when big thinkers gather to discuss life's eternal mysteries. To celebrate, today's image features the 'Body of Knowledge' sculpture at Goethe University in Frankfurt, Germany, which moulds steel letters from eight different alphabets into a human form. Spanish artist Jaume Plensa explains: 'Our body is the home of the spirit. The place in which ideas live.' On World Philosophy Day, we're all encouraged to look beyond easy answers and explore the questions that shape us, and the world around us.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KnowledgeSculpture_EN-IN5790560543_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KnowledgeSculpture_EN-IN5790560543_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Where ideas take shape","Title":"The \"Body of Knowledge\" sculpture by Jaume Plensa at Goethe University in Frankfurt, Germany","Copyright":"© Todamo/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.127805,8.667807/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.127805,8.667807;S9;Goethe University, Frankfurt&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261119_KnowledgeSculpture\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Philosophy+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261118_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261119_KnowledgeSculpture"},"Ssd":"20261119","Name":"KnowledgeSculpture","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"5790560543","FullDateString":"19 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These barn owls, bathed in evening light, are waiting for the hunt to begin. As night falls, these birds of prey swoop into action, listening for tiny movements in grasses or leaves made by mice and voles. Their heart-shaped faces help funnel sound into some of the sharpest ears in the animal kingdom. This allows them to locate their prey with pinpoint precision in the dark before swooping silently, their soft feathers muffling their approach. In autumn, young barn owls strike out to find their own territories. As the nights grow longer, you might spot them earlier in the evening, gliding over fields in search of supper.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_EN-IN2617869555_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_EN-IN2617869555_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Hunting from dusk till dawn","Title":"Pair of barn owls","Copyright":"© Zahoor Salmi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Barn owls don't hoot; they make eerie, screeching noises, which might explain their reputation as harbingers of doom.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Barn+owl&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261117_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite"},"Ssd":"20261118","Name":"BarnOwlsUnite","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"2617869555","FullDateString":"18 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today's image features the Trail of the Cedars, one of 1,126 kilometres of hiking trails in Glacier National Park, Montana. Its 1.4-km-long loop includes a raised boardwalk which cuts a path through western red cedars and hemlock trees. The park boasts routes for all abilities, taking in alpine lakes, wildflower meadows, mountain passes and wilderness stretching to the Canadian border.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_EN-IN2433074172_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_EN-IN2433074172_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Step into the great outdoors","Title":"Trail of the Cedars, Glacier National Park, Montana, USA","Copyright":"© DBushue Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.706957,-113.817235/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.706957,-113.817235;S9;Glacier National Park, Montana&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Trail+of+the+Cedars&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261116_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars"},"Ssd":"20261117","Name":"TrailCedars","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"2433074172","FullDateString":"17 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Incredible views and rock-solid foundations are part of the charm of these ancient dwellings, set into the cliffside in New Mexico. Nomads had long used the natural caves above Cliff Dweller Creek as temporary shelter, but it was the Native American Mogollon people who made them their home. Archaeologists believe they created dozens of rooms inside five alcoves in the 1270s and 1280s. Up to 15 families lived here at any one time, raising children, making pottery and overlooking the fertile Gila River valley where they grew crops and hunted wildlife. For reasons unknown, the Mogollon people moved on around 1300, leaving behind one of the American Southwest's most important archaeological sites.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_EN-IN2285530087_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_EN-IN2285530087_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Built to last","Title":"Gila Cliff Dwellings National Monument, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Chiara Salvadori/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/33.254028,-108.272634/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=33.254028,-108.272634;S9;Gila Cliff Dwellings National Monument, New Mexico&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Gila+Cliff+Dwellings+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261115_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff"},"Ssd":"20261116","Name":"GilaCliff","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"2285530087","FullDateString":"16 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As autumn's first frost sets in, ice crystals form on the leaves of evergreen shrubs, like this azalea. Long gone are the pinks, oranges and yellows of their spring blooms, but a new colourful display awaits, as their green leaves turn shades of red and purple. For the plants, the new pigments protect their leaves as temperatures drop, but for gardeners, they create a vibrant autumnal display, framed in white frost. When spring arrives, new growth will restore the shrub's green leaves and the colourful cycle begins anew.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FirstFrost_EN-IN2174706343_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FirstFrost_EN-IN2174706343_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Frosty foliage","Title":"Frozen azalea with red leaves","Copyright":"© avoferten/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The pigments that turn azalea leaves shades of red or purple are called anthocyanins.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261115_FirstFrost\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=azaleas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261114_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261115_FirstFrost"},"Ssd":"20261115","Name":"FirstFrost","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"2174706343","FullDateString":"15 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Welcome to Hong Kong, home to the world's largest collection of skyscrapers. Those pictured here tower above Victoria Harbour, whose deep waters allowed the island to develop as a busy trading port. Ships carrying tea, silk and other goods have passed through since the 1840s, but growth rocketed in the decades after World War II, fuelling a construction boom. With little flat land available between the harbour and the hills, developers had to build upwards, creating this distinctive skyline. In 2026, Hong Kong has 569 buildings above 150 metres high – more than any other city.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BlueHK_EN-IN1948913499_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BlueHK_EN-IN1948913499_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The only way is up","Title":"Victoria Harbour, Hong Kong, China","Copyright":"© Juan Romero/Cavan Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/22.285,114.165/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=22.285,114.165;S9;Victoria Harbour, Hong Kong&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261114_BlueHK\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Victoria+Harbour+Hong+Kong&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261113_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261114_BlueHK"},"Ssd":"20261114","Name":"BlueHK","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"1948913499","FullDateString":"14 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As the Sun dips towards the horizon, the Damodar River becomes a gathering place for Chhath Puja. The four-day Hindu festival is dedicated to Surya, the Sun God, and Chhathi Maiya. Mainly observed in Bihar, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh, as well as parts of Nepal, it is a celebration of gratitude for the Sun and its life-sustaining energy. Devotees observe fasting and gather beside rivers and other bodies of water to pray. One of the festival's most distinctive traditions is offering prayers to both the setting and rising sun, creating striking scenes as families and communities gather at the water's edge at dusk and dawn.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ChhathPuja2026_EN-IN1437573581_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ChhathPuja2026_EN-IN1437573581_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Glow of Chhath Puja","Title":"Sunset over the Damodar River during Chhath Puja","Copyright":"© ParthapratimMukherjee2056/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/23.480162,87.290903/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=23.480162,87.290903;S9;Damodar River&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261113_ChhathPuja2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Chhath+Puja&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261112_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261113_ChhathPuja2026"},"Ssd":"20261113","Name":"ChhathPuja2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"1437573581","FullDateString":"13 Nov, 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"दिन की छवि","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"अधिक जानें","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"त्वरित तथ्य:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"हाल ही की मुख पृष्ठ छवियाँ","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"{0} की मुख्य पृष्ठ छवि","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"इतिहास में आज के दिन","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"{0}, {1} में इस दिन","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"आज का Bing मुखपृष्ठ साझा करें","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"इस छवि को डाउनलोड करें. इस छवि का उपयोग केवल वॉलपेपर तक प्रतिबंधित है.","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERN